## Findings

Execution-r001 completed successfully with all 20 declared outputs freshly written. Focal arithmetic mean RPMs: cAMP P1 1.28665 to 19.5210 (15.172-fold), P2 411.767 to 3492.618 (8.482-fold), log2 response difference +0.83893. S16 KO P1 523.801 to 0.743490, P2 5855 to 194.909; log2 response difference -4.55169. Both signals co-move, while their relative magnitudes change. These are normalized RNA start signals, not initiation.

Important adverse result: primary control1 focal P1 is a source measured zero. Thus the no-pseudocount mean library log-ratio is undefined; it was not filled or discarded. All three cAMP libraries increase both signals relative to controls, but cAMP3 has a lower P1/P2 ratio than both positive-control libraries. The six finite unpaired cross-library ratio comparisons include two negatives. SOX10 has no focal zeros, all eight KO/control ratio comparisons are negative, and KO clones show large residual P1 variability. P1/(P1+P2) mean is 0.3265% to 0.5539% in primary cultures and 8.2111% to 0.3006% in S16. Adult nerves are 85.7931% for context only, not matched validation.

All positional windows are nonoverlapping and all selected Pmp22 intervals are nonoverlapping under either boundary convention. Main-table sensitivity differences retained the respective signs, but the full crossed low-signal × leave-one analysis is being reviewed before any strong robustness claim. Plp1 and Iars are absent from this selected table, not measured zero. Comparator coverage and exact source FDR tokens are retained; no new count model or p-value was fitted.

Execution-r002 completed successfully after reporting corrections (undefined-estimate denominators, no CV for log ratios, visible figure note for the zero) and lint. Scientific source values and estimation rules remain unchanged. Prior execution receipt remains preserved. Independent validator recomputed native-token/Decimal results and checked all response, sensitivity, leave-one, clone-family and comparator calculations: 129 checks passed; scripts pass ruff.

The crossed sensitivity check changes the conclusion: all 28 full-sample cAMP log-fold-of-means differences are positive (+0.0845 to +0.9051), but the 168 low-signal × window × leave-one variants span -0.3432 to +1.4333; removing the zero Control1 and adding 1 RPM reverses the preference. Thus a robust preferential cAMP P1 response is NOT established. By contrast all 168 SOX10 variants remain negative (-5.7178 to -3.1886 for log-fold-of-means difference; -5.7676 to -3.1524 for mean-library log-ratio change). This is a useful asymmetry/falsification of equally strong selectivity claims, not two equivalent positive findings.

Measured comparator sums support broad myelin/state changes: cAMP Mpz/Mbp rise (log2 +2.3785/+2.6275), Cnp nearly unchanged (+0.0489), Jun falls (-3.1644). SOX10 deletion lowers Mpz/Mbp (-10.5791/-6.6647), more strongly than total selected Pmp22 (-4.9264). The P1/P2 result is within-gene selectivity, not a PMP22-only perturbation. P1 stays a small share of primary-culture focal signal; adult nerve contrast remains context-confounded.

